---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import product from '../data/store.json';
import { dollars } from '../lib/money.js';

const email = product.contactEmail;
---

<Layout
  title="Shipping and returns"
  description="How shipping works and what happens if your shirt shows up wrong."
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Shipping and returns</h1>

      <h2>Shipping</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          {product.shippingLabel} is a flat {dollars(product.shippingCents)} per order, no matter how many shirts are in
          it. Orders of {dollars(product.freeShippingMinCents)} or more ship free.
        </li>
        <li>We ship to US addresses only for now.</li>
        <li>
          Every shirt is printed after you order it. Expect it at your door in about {product.shipMinDays} to {
            product.shipMaxDays
          } business days.
        </li>
        <li>Wrong address on your order? Email us right away and we'll fix it if it hasn't shipped yet.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Returns</h2>
      <p>
        Your shirt gets printed just for you, so we can't take returns or exchanges for the wrong size or a change of
        heart. Check the <a href="/size-chart/">size chart</a> before you order.
      </p>

      <h2>If something's wrong with it</h2>
      <p>
        If your shirt arrives damaged, misprinted, or it's not the one you ordered, that's on us. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
        within 30 days of delivery with a photo and the email address you used at checkout. We'll send a
        free replacement or refund you, your call.
      </p>

      <h2>Canceling an order</h2>
      <p>
        Email us as soon as you can. If your shirt hasn't gone to print yet, we'll cancel it and refund you in full.
        Once it's printed, it's yours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
